<h2>Where should the filter controls go on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">These are rough wireframes, not styled to the guidelines. The question is placement and how much is visible up front. Click one if you like, then answer in the terminal.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A. Filter bar above the table</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <h3 style="margin:0">Account activity</h3>
          <p style="margin:4px 0 10px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px">
            <div><div class="label">Event type</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:150px">All events &#9662;</div></div>
            <div><div class="label">Date range</div><div class="mock-input" style="width:130px">Last 90 days &#9662;</div></div>
            <label style="padding-bottom:6px"><input type="checkbox"> Failed sign-ins only</label>
            <span style="padding-bottom:6px;text-decoration:underline">Clear filters</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:0.85em">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Always-visible filter bar</h3>
      <p>Every control is on screen. The failed sign-in check is one click away, and so is the count. On a phone it wraps to three rows.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B. "Filter" button with a popover</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <h3 style="margin:0">Account activity</h3>
          <p style="margin:4px 0 10px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:6px">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter (1)</button>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:999px;padding:2px 8px;font-size:0.85em">Sign-in failed &#10005;</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.85em">Showing 6 of 48 events</span>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:8px;width:220px;margin-bottom:6px">
            <div class="label">Event type</div><div class="mock-input">Sign-in failed &#9662;</div>
            <div class="label" style="margin-top:6px">Date range</div><div class="mock-input">Last 90 days &#9662;</div>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Popover</h3>
      <p>The page stays tidy, and active filters show as removable tags. Finding a failed sign-in takes two or three clicks instead of one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C. Quick-filter chips</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <h3 style="margin:0">Account activity</h3>
          <p style="margin:4px 0 10px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px">
            <span class="mock-button">All</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:2px 8px">Failed sign-ins</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:2px 8px">Sign-ins</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:2px 8px">Security changes</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;padding:2px 8px">Settings</span>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:0.85em">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Chips for groups of types</h3>
      <p>Fastest to scan. But it groups the nine types into buckets we'd have to define, and no component in 02 fits it well, so reviewers may push back.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
